Shawn Aaron McKisson (shawn@cs.utexas.edu) wrote:
: I am trying to run mosaic from a VXT 2000+ X terminal, but get the error
: message "Can't open display." when trying to do so. Oddly enough,
: this error message does not appear from the master terminal on the Alpha.

You bumped into something called "X Server security". On every X Server
you have to state which systems and users are permitted to access your X
Server (i.e. display). Look for an entry called "Security" in your
terminal manager menu, and enter the appropriate information. Beware that
when using TCPIP as a transport, you'll have to enter a "*" in the Username
field (thereby permitting all users from that node access to your VXT -
that's the way it is with basic TCPIP).

Hope it helps,
  Martin
