In article <1996Jun29.181726.16031@decus.org.au>,  <manson@decus.org.au> wrote:
>In article <4r11ng$30m@mksrv1.dseg.ti.com>, dittman@hibernia.dseg.ti.com (Eric Dittman) writes:
>> I have a VAXstation 3100 model 30 with the 8 plane graphics board (GPX).
>> T 50 shows the following:
>> 
>>  ? 8PLN      0007.0213  V1.3
>> 
>> Unfortunately, I don't have any manuals with information on interpreting
>> the test codes.  I have a VR260 connected to the system and it looks okay
>> but the VR260 is only B&W so I'm not sure.
>
>Like you, I don't have the manuals either, so I can't tell you positively
>what the code means, but......as a wild guess, you don't have 75 ohmn
>terminalors on the Red and Blue of the RGB connectors. (Assuming you've
>got the colour cable)
>
>A single ? usually means there is something not right, but the double ??
>means it's really broke.  Does the thing work?

  He says it looks ok, so I think the single ? is not serious.

> 
>> Does anyone know what this error code means?
>> 

   MY 3100/38 manual says the 0007 is the status of the failing test
and can be ignored.  the 021 indicates the failing test is "Video readback"
and the 3 indicates a "status message" rather than no error (1) or fatal
error (2).  Perhaps you're right in that it's the 75 ohm terminators.  I 
know the SPX graphics board gives a similar (don't remember the exact
error) when the monitor connector isn't connected upon bootup.

