Shawn Aaron McKisson (shawn@cs.utexas.edu) wrote:
: I am trying to run mosaic from a VXT 2000+ X terminal, but get the error
: message "Can't open display." when trying to do so. Oddly enough,
: this error message does not appear from the master terminal on the Alpha.
: What can be done to fix this problem?

You have to say     mosaic -display yourmachine:0
that tells mosaic to display on your window rather than the one on that the
program is physically running on.   You also have to use the xhost command,

On your machine (the one you are logged on from), use the xhost command:

xhost +

I'm assuming mosaic is running on another machine and putting the display on
your machine.  Your machine won't allow other machines to display stuff on
your window unless you allow it to (this is to prevent other people on remote
machine from just putting garbage on your screen that you cant get rid of).
xhost +    allows other machines to display on your window.  xhost +  allows
all machines to display on your window.  A  safer way would be:
xhost + machinename     where machinename is the name of the machine running
mosaic.

(BTW, this is valid on all machines, not just for DEC machines)




