The LA50 is indeed a serial printer. It is RS232C and RS423 compatible. 
Here are the signals used:

Function        Direction     Pin      RS-232 mnemonic

recv data       to printer    3        BB
Send data       from printer  2        BA
Terminal ready  from printer  20       CD
RTS             from printer  4        CA
busy/ready      from printer  11       -
prot. ground    from printer  1        -
signal ground   common        7        AB

Also there are some dip-switches inside behind the front panel to control 
character sets, baud rate and such like. I think the factory defaults for 
the printer are 4800 baud, 8 bits no parity.

email if you need more info on the switch settings.

