Been there. Done that.  It works.

If you choose the "LA75 (Microsoft)" driver, then change the printer from
LA75 to "other" on the printer front panel.  The LA75 WIN95 drivers uses
the PROPRINTER mode.  You can make this change permament on your printer
by holding the setup button while powering on.  This gets you into the
setup mode. Use the other front panel buttons to scroll the settings and
toggle the mode to Other.

If you want to have it as a true LA75 (why?) then you can use the WIN 3.x
driver.  You will need the Digital version of win 3.1 and the last two
disks.  Use the "Have disk" option to load the printer.  When it complains
about not finding some files slip in either the last WIN 3.1 disks or the
next to last disk.  You will have to switch between the disks a couple of
times (or if you know the files it needs, you can put them on a directory
on your c drive).  I had to do this for my Digital LN03 serial printer.

I have both the LA75 and the LN03 on an A/B switch connected to COM1. 
Both printers set to 9600 8 data 1 stop Xon/Xoff.

Ignore all the stuff from another reply about DMA, IRQ, etc.  This is just
a simple serial printer (but you and I know that).  Email me if you can't
get it going.  I just now did the LA75 Micrsoft in less than 5 minutes (I
rebuilt 95 awhile back and never got around to reloading the LA75). 
Print test page works great.

