Tim Shoppa wrote:
> 
> In article <31C6F216.41C6@relay.nswc.navy.mil>,
> A. J. Corda <acorda@relay.nswc.navy.mil> wrote:
> >          I've noticed that the TK50 drive that's already
> >       there uses an IDC 26-pin connector that goes
> >       to what looks like a TK50 (Q-bus?)
> 
> The 26-pin connector is not the Q-bus, it's just the connector
> to the TK50.  There's a controller that connects the 26-pin cable
> to the Q-bus, called the TQK50.  There's also a controller that
> connects the TK50 to the Unibus, called the TUK50.  And then there's
> the controller you have, that connects the TK50 to the SCSI bus.
> 
> > to SCSI adaptor
> >       card mounted along with the drive in the enclosure.
> >       The TK70 drive that I happened across also seems to
> >       have the same 26-pin (Q-bus?) connector. Is it really
> >       the same interface?  i.e. is the SCSI adaptor card
> >       capable of handling a TK70?
> 
> No, this particular SCSI card is not capable of handling a TK70.  The
> TK70 format, while similar to the TK50, has a higher data density
> and more tracks.  There is a card that does what you want, but I don't
> know what it's exact part number is.
> 

Thanks for the response... Does anyone out there happen to know
the part # for the SCSI-to-TK70 adaptor card, and/or where I could
get hold of one?

					-Thanks again...
					-al
					-acorda@relay.nswc.navy.mil



