In article <4ps1fl$kie@medulla.ama.ttuhsc.edu>, sean@cortex (Sean Dougherty) writes:

>I have some Micropolis 3243 that I'm trying to wedge into a DEC 3000 
>running Digital UNIX V3.2C.  Does anyone have the disktab entry for this? 
>Or know where I might find it?

For disks that are well behaved, the Digital UNIX disklabel command
will can get the geometry from the drive and a default partition table
from the driver.  Once the disk has been labeled, the newfs command
will get the geometry from the label.  As example:

# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c micropolis

filling, in the # for the right device number.

--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com




