OpenVMS Customer,

NOTE:  If you have received previous mail from Sheila Mulvey regarding 
the OpenVMS V7.1-EFT1 SDK, and you are already on the list to receive
it, please disregard this message.

Digital will be distributing an OpenVMS V7.1-EFT1 SDK (Software 
Developer Kit). The SDK contains early releases of the OpenVMS
V7.1 VAX and Alpha operating systems.  The kit will allow OpenVMS 
software developers early access to the new features of V7.1, 
including DECnet/OSI and OpenVMS Cluster enhancements.  

In addition to the operating system, users can also test compatible
layered product kits that will be made available on the Internet at
the same time.  

The SDK package contains all necessary firmware, documentation, 
and temporary product authorization keys (PAKs) necessary to take 
full advantage of V7.1.  The temporary PAKs will allow use of the 
software until January 1997.  The SDK kit is scheduled to be 
shipped in early July 1996.  The final product will be made 
available 2HFCY96.

The SDK software will run on all Alpha and VAX systems currently
shipping.  The SDK is intended for development testing only.  It
should not be used in a production environment.

Support for SDK users will be through an Internet newsgroup 
(vmsnet.sdk.openvms.fieldtest) to report problems, make comments, 
etc.  An engineering support team will monitor the newsgroup and 
address any issues.

The SDK can be used for demo purposes, for customers in your area, 
sales events, International DECUS events, etc. 

The following is a list of the software products contained in this
kit and their shipping status:

  Product                            Status
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  OpenVMS Alpha V7.1-EFT1            Field Test
  OpenVMS VAX V7.1-EFT1              Field Test
  DECnet/OSI V7.1                    Field Test                  
  DECnet Phase IV V7.1-EFT1          Field Test
  DEC TCP/IP V4.1-EFT1               Field Test
  DECwindows Motif V1.2-4            Shipping Product           

  

