Jit Leng - PSA wrote:
> 
> Try the following :
> Select your network adapter as "DEC Etherworks 3 (All ISA versions)"
> with the following resources settings:-
> I/O address range :- 300 - 31F
> Interrupt         :- 5
> Memory Address    :- D0000 - D07FF
> 
> Dr Andrew P Harris (harrisa@logica.com) wrote:
> : I'm installing Windows 95 on a machine which has a DEC 205 network adapter.
> : Windows 95 installs okay but doesn't detect the card automatically.  I've
> : managed to install the drivers from the Windows 95 CD-ROM but it still doesn't
> : work presumably because it hasn't been configured properly.  Does anyone know
> : how the card should be configured or offer any other advice which may help.

> : Andy (harris@logica.com).


Boy, I fought with this same problem for a day and a half this week and the answer 
was so simple.  

First, do as Jit said, use the Etherworks 3 (ISA all versions) driver.  BTW, Win95 
did automatically recognize it.  Now heres what I did...I wrote down all of the 
autoconfiguration setting that WIN95's device manager set up for it.  Then I ran 
NIC SETUP (which comes on the DE205 driver disk) and looked at the settings that 
were stored in NVRAM on the 205.  I matched these settings to what WIN95 
autoconfigured (except for IRQ and Memory window 2K) saved it and Voila! 

Jeff

