Hi al,

funny challenge that we encounter on our site:

For years we're running LAVC over ethernet and FDDI, Vaxes and Alpha's are 
connected by a common ethernet and by an FDDI ring. PEdriver is supposed to 
choose between the two circuits and it does so regarding two criteria:
1-packetsize: it favors large packetsize networks (FDDI)
2-latency: it favors minimum latency circuits

What happens? We now connect the VAX/Alpha systems on an ethernet switch by 
which we garantuee that a 64 byte packet is delivered in 64 microsec. 
Although the max packet size of our ethernet circuit is 1498 in comparison 
with the more-than-4000 byte FDDI-circuit, the PEdriver tends to like the 
ethernet more than it likes FDDI, we can only force volume shadowing over 
FDDI by enlarging ethernet latency between the Vaxes/Alpha's (By connecting 
several cascaded switches in between).

Ever heard of such a problem? Help will be greatly appreciated!! Rather 
ironic: first the system engineers always wining about bigger bandwidht, 
faster circuits and now they're asking me to give them more latency (..)

Thanks in advance
