In article <31C08DE9.2E8B@global.co.za>,  <hhwill@global.co.za> wrote:
>Hi all
>
>Anyone know from which version RSX supported large SCSI disks?

That depends on your definition of "large" :-)

ODS-1 support for disks larger than 256 Megabytes was added somewhere around
RSX-11M V4.0 or V4.1.  I have used unpartitioned SCSI disks as large
as 2 gigabytes with RSX11M+ V4.2, but I wouldn't be surprised if something
prevented you from using volumes larger than 4 gigabytes.

The SCSI disk issue isn't realy relevant here; SCSI disks almost
universally emulate MSCP disks, and RSX never knows they are actually
SCSI. 

>And which SCSI controllers support tape and disk off the same SCSI port.

I only have two data points:

1.  The Emulex UC07 and UC08 require that all devices on the same SCSI
bus be either tape or disk.

2.  The CMD CQD440 allows you to mix tapes and disks on the same SCSI
bus.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



