Yes, floppy drives used it. But it IS present with most hard drives, as
far back as MFM. The reason why SCSI usually disables it is that SCSI
doesn't use the same mechanism to present itself to the system. The method
in the old PCs allows for a primary and secondary controller with two
drives each. SCSI didn't fit. SCSI using a DMA channel could result in a
conflict, because they can't take the one from the main hard drive
controller because they don't know if SCSI drives are the only drives in
the system.

