>Is there a way to create a "ram" drive using the memory of the alpha?
>

Yes.  See the newfs(8) manual page, which doubles as the mfs(8) manual
page.  The mfs command will create a file system in memory.  Oh, this
only applies to Digital UNIX, but since you didn't mention the operating
system...

What you will need to be aware of is that the file system uses paged
memory.  If the system has plenty of free memory, then there probably
won't be any paging, but there could be.

>The people here have an application that the think they can speed up if 
>it reads and writes to memory.  I have never heard anyone doing this on a 
>VAX machine.

Ah, maybe you're not running Digital UNIX.  I've heard rumors of a
ram disk driver for OpenVMS, but I don't know if it ever got turned
into a product.
