> 15 Sandcroft Avenue, Uphill,              Fax: +44 1934 629798
> Somerset, BS23 4SS, United Kingdom.       Mob: +44  802 820213
> mailto:ian.reid@cityscape.co.uk    http://www.cityscape.co.uk/users/fp75
> --------------------------------------------------------------------The Pathworks client has had inherent Netware connectivity support since
version 5.  Before then, it would coexist.  I used this in version 5.0
with good luck, though it would not use VLMs which I prefer.  It may 
now, I haven't been back to it for over a year.

If you need Novell clients to reach the Vax, you can try Pathworks for 
OpenVMS (Netware).  I found Digital's new implementations of Pathworks 
a little sad; they were essentially doing a rewrite from ver 4.2, and 
opted to go to something virtually identical to Lan Manager for an 
administration interface.  Face it folks, Lan Manager hardly has the 
network world by the tale; it's dated.  I'm not saying the new 
Pathworks isn't an acceptable product; merely that it could have been 
better.  

Check out a company called TGV.  They were recently bought by Cisco,
and have been producing a product called Multinet for years.  It's TCPIP 
for the Vax, but they offer a Novell connectivity product as well.  If 
it's half as good as the TCPIP, it'll beat Digital's.

Regards,
Kevin



