> to do anything.  If I try a MOUNT or an INIT, it comes back with "device
> is offline", though a "$Sho Dev" shows it online.  I've tried some things
> at the SCSI level, but without any luck.

This is pretty common, though it has gotten to be less so since VMS V6.1
(or was it 6.0?).  Anyway, the VMS SCSI disk drivers (DKDRIVER) are 
fairly picky about the SCSI implementations they will talk to properly.
Witness, for example, that it used to be (and may still be) impossible
to get the vanilla DKDRIVER to work with some Magneto-Optical SCSI drives.

One thing that I have found is the MODISK driver from Acorn Software, whose
FTP site has free eval copies of their software at ftp.acornsw.com.  I
had success using this to access very old Quantum hard drives that DKDRIVER
wouldn't touch.  Likewise, MODISK did a find job letting me access my Sony
MO disk, so who knows?  Maybe it would work on the Bernoulli.

What I want to know is, has anyone ever tried hooking up an IOMEGA ZIP
or JAZ drive to a VMS machine, either via DKDRIVER or MODISK?  

