Subject: SPARCStorage Array Problems and Alternatives

DISCLAIMER:

Your experiences with the Sun SPARCStorage Array can, may, and probably 
will differ. The purpose of this article to gather information regarding
other users experiences, it is in no way intended to attack any single
vendors product or services.

I take NO responsibility for any assumptions or views drawn from this 
article and its subsequent discussion.

RESPONSES:

Please email your responses to dbemis@teleport.com. I will summarize the 
responses as whole in a week.

Goals:

1. Determine if other Sun customers are experiencing problems with 
SPARCStorage Arrays. If so, what is the nature of their problems and 
how are they approaching the issues.

2. Determine alternative hardware and software approaches Sun 
customers use to address the reason why we have SPARCStorage Arrays -- 
"large" disk subsystem, high availability, and performance.

Questions:

1. For those Sun users with SPARCStorage Arrays, if you have 
experienced problems, especially disk failures, with your SPARCStorage 
Arrays I would like to know about the type of problems, your 
configuration, and how Sun worked with you to address the issues?

2. For those Sun users who have addressed their disk requirements with 
another disk vendor, I would like to know why you chose that other vendor? 
Additionally, it would be helpful to know how difficult it is to use this 
other vendor's equipment, what your support experiences have been like, and 
how often patches and fixes have to be applied to support their product?  
Our initial research leans towards looking into DEC's and Data General's 
array offerings. We may consider EMC**2 offerings. 

3. Even if you are not a Sun customer, yet you use a DEC, Data General, or 
EMC**2 array offerings, I would like to hear if any of these vendors 
provide exceptionally good or bad products and/or support.

Background:

The following list profiles our systems which use SPARCStorage Arrays:

Processors			S20s, S1000s
SPARCStorage Arrays		Model 101s, 102s, and 112s
Disks				1.05GB and 2.1GB
OS				Solaris 2.3 - 2.4
Array Firmware Level		3.4 - 3.6
Disk Firmware Level		<=416
Filesystem Software		ODS 4.0, Veritas 2.1, and Veritas 2.1.1

We do not encapsulate our root disks. We do stripe and mirror our 
disks extensively.

We are a global company and we are experiencing problems with 
SPARCStorage Arrays on a worldwide basis. The types of problems follow:

- Read & write errors.
- Tracking errors.
- Controller failures.
- Fibre card failures.
- Disk failures in a mirrored configuration crashing or hanging an array.

Any relevant information is appreciated.

Thank you.


--
