Probably it is simplest if you take the chip containing the address
from the old board. Or get an licence update for your software.

> I tried to write a small program that set it with a SIOCSPHYSADDR
> ioctl, but hung my workstation instead. If anyone has such a program
> I hope to avoid the debug-run-reboot-debug-run-reboot cycle :-)

I think this will not work. SIOCRPHYSADDR will always get the true
"hardware" address. For example, it will still return 08-00-2b-* in
spite of Decnet running (which modifies the physical address to
aa-00-04-*).

You could of course also patch the binary and remove the check for the
physical address. That ioctl should be relatively easy to find. ;-)

