X-Deja-AN: 158737106
references: <4ov588$gqr@web.cae.ca>
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
organization: University of Massachusetts, Amherst
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
x-mailer: Mozilla 1.22 (Windows; I; 16bit)


raindos is used on an ibm that will format 1.2 meg 5 1/4 floppies.
place the line:
device=c:\raindos.sys
in the autoexec.bat file, and place raindos and th other unzipped files
on your root C directory.
Your computer (IBM compatible) will now assign another drive letter to 
the 5 1/4 floppy.
put in double density floppies (360k), and type "format d:," or whatever
drive letter it is assigned.
this formats the floppies for use by the decmate (think of this as 
"Fdisk" on a harddrive).

You need another program called teledisk from update. 
all the files there have .td0 as the suffix, and td0's are compressed 
disk images for the teledisk program.
download the .td0's you want, then type teledisk and use it to write to 
the 5 1/4 floppies.

WPS is a neato-keen easy to use word processing program. If there is no
spell check disk at update.uu.se, then try the other main source under 
pdp8 files; sunsite, I think.

If you have questions, email at
jboldway@student.umass.edu
P.S. you don't need to run raindos if you run teledisk.




