re TLZ07s

    As far as I know there are 2 seperate service issues with them. The 
first is that if you have a TLZ07-VA and intend to install it in asystem 
that can handle SCSI wide (like a BA362) then it requires a "special" 
connector in the rear of the VA enclosure. The problem is that as of this 
writing DEC doesn't have a special order number for TLZ07s in wide boxes 
so ... it's a crap shoot and you'd better have feild service standing 
by.(if you have the wrong connector it will hang the entire SCSI bus) The 
second issue is with firmware. Apparently DEC just released a new version 
but field service doesn't have the update tape yet and as a result 
getting a TLZ07 through your local logistics will take over a week !!!


    For what it's worth the TLZ06s had lots of firmware problems when 
they were first released as well (unknown media format errors)


Brian V




