I am running Polycenter HSM v1.2 for VMS on VMS 6.1, using a TZ877
in compressed mode on a Alpha Server 2100 in HSM Plus mode.
We have discovered the following problems:

If you are shelving a file at the time the Alpha Server crashes, the
tape currently being used is checkpointed - meaning the tape is nolonger
available for further shelved files, and the next tape is used.  The
second problem is that the file being shelved is sometimes truncated, 
even though it was not entirely written to the tape.  Through numerous 
tests, I have been able to determine that the tape does not contain 
a logical end of tape mark (two consective eof marks).

Even if I fix, the logical end of tape - by moving to the end of tape
(which errors) then backup to the point after the previous backup
saveset eof headers, then set a new (second) eof mark, the problem
when HSM starts up, is that the previous requests are checked, then when
HSM finds that the last file is not there, it checkpoints the tape,
and starts using the next tape.
  
Now, a TZ87 can hold upto 20GB.  I have had a tape checkpointed with
only about 2GB on it.  This cuts the potential capacity of the TZ877
by almost 15% (from 140GB to 122GB).  If this happens twice, then
you might as well start over.

My question is: is there any method that would allow you to UNCHECKPOINT
a tape in PLUS mode and set the file position to the proper location.
I know this seems real time consumming for a $40.00 tape,  but it is
the nearline capacity of the archive that I am trying to maintain at
the highest level possible.

